# === QA-Agent project sync .gitignore (generated) ===
# SUT credentials — KHÔNG BAO GIỜ commit (B15 environment.json holds
# base_url + username/password/token in plaintext).
environment.json
environment.json.bak
# B4 draft layer — unreviewed working state, collides noisily across testers.
.draft/
# Sync staging snapshots (ephemeral) — EXCEPT the deletion ledger, which is
# shared state (a tester's intentional archive/delete must propagate to every
# puller). So we ignore the whole .sync/ dir but un-ignore the ledger file.
.sync/*
!.sync/deletions.json
# Regenerable / per-machine / internal artifacts.
exports/
excel_imports/
screenshots/
reports/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
_pw_profiles/
# Backups produced by atomic_write (.bak) — recoverable from git history.
*.bak
# Backup suffix used by sync_update_runner._mirror_nonsemantic_files and
# _copy_document_dir when a non-semantic local file diverges from remote.
# Without this rule, git add -A stages these dead backups, shipping them to
# the shared remote where every puller re-backs them up (.local_bak.local_bak …).
*.local_bak
trace_graph.json.bak
session_log.jsonl.bak*
# trace_graph.json is a derived artifact (rebuilt from source JSON on mtime
# change). Committing it only ships dead weight: the pull side discards it via
# _is_stale (mtime differs across machines) and rebuilds locally anyway. Keeping
# it out of git avoids huge meaningless diffs / merge conflicts.
trace_graph.json
# manifest.json (project-root document index) is likewise a derived index — it
# is rebuilt by sync_update._rebuild_manifest_from_docmeta from the on-disk
# documents/*/meta.json after every pull. Two testers each ingesting a doc would
# otherwise produce a meaningless conflict here. The authoritative per-doc
# meta.json files ARE synced (under documents/), so the index regenerates.
#
# IMPORTANT: anchor with a leading slash so ONLY the ROOT manifest.json is
# ignored. Without it, git treats "manifest.json" as a path-segment pattern
# matching at every depth, which would ALSO ignore ``scripts/manifest.json``
# (the script↔testcase linkage manifest — a SOURCE-OF-TRUTH, NOT derived).
# That silent over-match starved pullers of the script manifest: the Scripts
# tab then showed "no manifest" + prompted an unnecessary Migrate that wiped
# publisher-accumulated linkages/generated_from anchors.
/manifest.json
# Per-user agent runtime.
agent_workspace/
chat_sessions/
